# What tools/bench/Dockerfile is built from, as an allowlist: everything is left
# out, then the files the image needs are let back in. tools/bench_in_container.py
# builds from a copy of the committed tree and puts this file at that copy's
# root as both .dockerignore and .containerignore, so Docker and Podman read the
# same list. BuildKit also finds it here, beside the Dockerfile.
**
!pyproject.toml
!README.md
!LICENSE
!MANIFEST.in
!requirements
!src
!tests
!build-inputs/
!build-inputs/cubeprogrammer.zip
!tools/
!tools/bench/
!tools/bench/install_cubeprogrammer.sh
!tools/bench/cubeprogrammer-auto-install.xml
# The tier copies, builds and flashes this demo, and builds its own images out
# of it.
!examples/nucleo-f446re_demo
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info
**/.pytest_cache
examples/nucleo-f446re_demo/build
examples/nucleo-f446re_demo/.agentic-hil
